{title: At Calvary (I Am Free)}
{artist: William R. Newell, C. Michael Pilato / Daniel B. Towner, C. Michael Pilato}
{genre: Modern Worship, Hymn}
{style: Contemporary}
{flow: Response}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 98}
{time: 4/4}
{license: Public domain}
{c: Words: William R. Newell (1895) and C. Michael Pilato (2014). Music: Daniel B. Towner (1895) and C. Michael Pilato (2014). Released into the public domain by C. Michael Pilato · Source: https://github.com/cmpilato/worship-music/tree/main/At_Calvary_I_Am_Free}
{c: Chords from the writer's own lead sheet (MusicXML in the source above)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]Years I spent in vanity and pride,
[F]Caring not my Lord was [Bb]crucified,
[Gm]Knowing not it was for [Ebadd2]me He died on [Fsus]Cal[F]va[Bb]ry.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]By God's Word at last my sin I learned,
[F]Then I trembled at the [Bb]law I'd spurned,
[Gm]Till my guilty soul im[Ebadd2]ploring turned to [Fsus]Cal[F]va[Bb]ry.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[Eb]Mercy there was great and [Bb]grace was free.
[F]Pardon there was multi[Bb]plied to [Bb/D]me.
[Eb]There my burdened soul found [Bb]liberty at [Fsus]Cal[F]va[Bb]ry!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Bb]Oh the love that drew salvation's plan!
[F]Oh the grace that brought it [Bb]down to man!
[Gm]Oh the mighty gulf that [Ebadd2]God did span at [Fsus]Cal[F]va[Bb]ry!
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge}
[F]I am free. [Ebmaj7]I am free.
[Bb/D]By the mer[Cm7]cy of God's [Bb/D]great grace, [Eb]I am free.
[F]I am free [Ebmaj7](and I am forgiven). I am free [Bb/D](and now I am living).
By the mer[Cm7]cy of God's [Bb/D]great grace, [Eb]I am free.
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Bb]Now I give to Jesus everything.
[F]Now I gladly own Him [Bb]as my King.
[Gm]Now my raptured soul can [Ebadd2]only sing of [Fsus]Cal[F]va[Bb]ry!
{end_of_verse}
